all involves every emotion that's  possible to a human being in the course  of 60 minutes I think you can probably  be touched by any emotion you can think  of a short of childbirth and we're  working on that but that's I guess my my  prime reason for it because to this very  day you can see on the playground which  one of the little fellas is suddenly  squared his shoulders and bowed his neck  and will go on and try to express  himself over the opponent and that's  that's life it's competitive  it has all of the competitive elements  of making living and raising a family  and all of that why do people still  think that you said whoa Nellie I got it  from my grandfather great-grandfather  Jefferson Davis Robert  who was not a large fellow but he was a  very good farmer and he was always  working on something with his hands and  creating things to make his life a  little easier but he had a little bit of  a temper underneath that hat that he  wore all the time and when he would get  frustrated or drop something or break  something many times I heard him say as  he had that half whistle that so many  people seem to have back in those days  where he wasn't really a whistle it was  just sort of a kind of and grandpa would  would break something and I could hear  him say oh I thought that there were  times when you people kept saying all  say well Nelly or there was one  expression that you were given credit  for that I thought you tried to distance  yourself from was there one or am I  forgetting something here yeah I thought  for some reason that you were saying you  didn't say well Nelly and then I I know  you'd say yeah different phrases but for  some reason I thought people were trying  to pin that on on you with whoa Nelly  but if it's yours then I apologize well  I didn't and also did you were you up  for doing the miracle and ice doing the  hockey broadcast during the 1980 Winter  Olympics that Al Michaels did were you  part of that decision at all yes I was  abs